{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Android Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors Kotlin source files for changes and provides automated analysis of code quality, module boundary violations, threading issues, and Android-specific best practices.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.kt",
      "**/*.kts",
      "**/src/**/*.kt"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A Kotlin source file has been modified in the HexScroll Android project. Please analyze the changes for:\n\n1. **Module Boundaries**: core:domain must not import android.* or androidx.room.*; core:designsystem must not import domain or data packages\n2. **Threading**: WindowManager calls must be on Dispatchers.Main; Room DAO calls must be on Dispatchers.IO\n3. **Overlay Safety**: Any ComposeView added to WindowManager must use OverlayLifecycleOwner and advance lifecycle through ON_CREATE, ON_START, ON_RESUME in order\n4. **KSP Usage**: Ensure no kapt annotations are used; all annotation processing uses KSP\n5. **Coroutine Scope**: Check for GlobalScope usage which should be avoided; prefer viewModelScope or serviceScope\n6. **Null Safety**: Flag any !! operators that could be replaced with safer alternatives\n7. **Code Smells**: Long functions, duplicate logic, missing error handling in try/catch blocks\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions while respecting the existing clean architecture pattern."
  }
}
